# Ephemerate (CR 702.88a): "Exile target creature you control, then return it to the battlefield under its owner's
# control." Cast from the hand it is exiled as it resolves instead of going to the graveyard, and at the beginning of
# its controller's next upkeep may be cast from exile without paying its mana cost.
#
# Bot1 casts Thraben Inspector on turn 1 (a Clue), and Ephemerate on it on turn 3: the Inspector returns as a new
# object (CR 400.7) and investigates again (a second Clue), and Ephemerate waits in exile rather than the graveyard.
# On turn 5, Bot1's next upkeep, Bot1 casts it from exile for nothing and blinks the Inspector once more (a third
# Clue). That cast was not from a hand, so Ephemerate is put into the graveyard as it resolves and does not rebound.

